.TH TELCOSEC 1 "September 2026" "TelcoChiselOS 3.0" "TelcoSec User Commands"
.SH NAME
telcosec, telcochisel \- Unified Operator CLI for Telecom Security, SDR Diagnostics, and 5G Core Operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B telcosec
.RB [ COMMAND ]
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B telcochisel
.RB [ COMMAND ]
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B telcosec
is the official operator command center and system diagnostic utility for
.B TelcoChiselOS
and Debian/Ubuntu-derived Linux distributions.
.PP
Designed specifically for telecommunications security auditors, cellular network penetration testers, and Software Defined Radio (SDR) researchers,
.B telcosec
provides zero-dependency static inspection of kernel parameters, hardware transceivers, network buffers, and cellular core lifecycle daemons.
.PP
The command provides native discovery and optimization without relying on Python or external runtimes, querying Linux kernel subsystems directly via
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
and system PAM limits.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR check ", " status
Execute a comprehensive pre-flight audit of kernel scheduler architecture (detecting low-latency or real-time PREEMPT_RT patches), distribution flavor, PAM real-time priority limits, high-throughput USBFS memory allocation, hugepages reservation, reverse path filtering mode, and telecom systemd service daemons.
.TP
.BR hardware ", " hw ", " devices
Enumerate and actively probe all connected radio, modem, and smartcard hardware. Dispatches diagnostic checks across SoapySDR, Ettus UHD, Nuand BladeRF, and PC/SC smartcard readers.
.TP
.BI search " <query>"
Search the catalog of 100 pre-installed telecommunications security tools and desktop entries by protocol keyword, acronym, or binary name (e.g., \fBsctp\fR, \fBdiameter\fR, \fB5g\fR, \fBnas\fR, \fBopen5gs\fR).
.TP
.B docs
Open the interactive operator documentation portal. If the local offline documentation bundle is present at \fI/usr/share/doc/telcosec/index.html\fR, it launches in the default web browser; otherwise, it falls back to the online documentation portal at \fBhttps://telcochisel.com\fR.
.TP
.BR sdr " [" status "|" usb "|" 10g "|" firmware "]"
Manage Software Defined Radio transceiver driver frameworks and hardware interfaces.
.RS
.TP
.B status
Inspect connected USB SDR transceivers and serial AT cellular modems.
.TP
.B usb
Verify and tune the kernel USBFS memory allocation (\fIusbfs_memory_mb\fR) to prevent sample drops during high MSPS captures.
.TP
.B 10g
Inspect and configure 10Gbps SFP+ network interfaces for network SDRs.
.TP
.B firmware
Audit local offline FPGA bitstream caches for BladeRF (\fI.rbf\fR) and Ettus USRP (\fI.bin\fR) devices.
.RE
.TP
.BR 10g " [" status "|" tune "|" setup "|" probe "]"
Optimize 10Gbps SFP+ Ethernet transceivers for high-bandwidth Ettus USRP transceivers (USRP X310, N310).
.RS
.TP
.B status
Display interface MTU, operational link state, negotiated link speed, and kernel socket buffer sysctl parameters.
.TP
.BI tune " <interface>"
Apply high-performance network tuning: sets MTU to 9000 (Jumbo Frames), maximizes RX/TX ring descriptors to 4096 via \fBethtool\fR, and sizes kernel socket buffers (\fIrmem_max\fR, \fIwmem_max\fR) to 64 MB.
.TP
.BI setup " <interface> [" preset "]"
Configure IP address and subnet for USRP transceivers using predefined presets (\fBx310-0\fR, \fBx310-1\fR, \fBn310-0\fR, \fBn310-1\fR) and apply 10GbE tuning.
.TP
.BI probe " [" ip "]"
Probe the local network or a specific IP address for connected Ettus USRP devices using \fBuhd_find_devices\fR.
.RE
.TP
.B firmware
Display cached offline SDR FPGA images located in \fI/usr/share/Nuand/bladeRF\fR and \fI/usr/share/uhd/images\fR.
.TP
.BR profile " [" lab "|" field "|" status "]"
Display or switch operational networking profiles:
.RS
.TP
.B lab
Disables IPv4 reverse path filtering (\fIrp_filter=0\fR) across all network interfaces, allowing packet crafting, asymmetric routing, and raw telecom frame injection.
.TP
.B field
Enforces strict reverse path filtering (\fIrp_filter=1\fR) and enables firewall protections for live field engagements.
.TP
.B status
Display the currently active profile.
.RE
.TP
.BR pkg " [" list "|" info "|" install "|" remove "|" check "|" repo "]"
Manage the official 10-tier modular TelcoChisel telecom security metapackages:
.RS
.TP
.BR list " [" \-\-json "]"
List all 10 canonical domain metapackage suites with local installation status and descriptions.
.TP
.BI info " <alias_or_name>"
Display detailed tool breakdown, dependencies, and subsystem components for a requested suite (e.g. \fB5g\fR, \fBsdr\fR, \fBsim\fR, \fBwireline\fR).
.TP
.BI install " <alias_or_name>"
Install a modular domain suite using the system package manager.
.TP
.BI remove " <alias_or_name>"
Remove a domain suite from the local system.
.TP
.B check
Audit installed metapackages and verify dpkg database package consistency.
.TP
.BR repo " [" status "|" enable "]"
Audit or configure enrollment in the official \fBhttps://meta.telcochisel.com\fR APT repository and GPG signing keys.
.RE
.TP
.BR sim " [" status "|" readers "|" atr "|" trace "|" lpac "|" shell "]"
Comprehensive smartcard, SIM, and eSIM auditing suite:
.RS
.TP
.B status
Display global SIM auditing environment status, including PC/SC daemon state, attached readers, and toolchain readiness.
.TP
.B readers
Enumerate attached PC/SC and USB CCID smartcard readers, card presence status, and detected ATR strings.
.TP
.BI atr " [" hex_string "]"
Decode and analyze an ISO/IEC 7816-3 Answer-to-Reset (ATR) sequence. If \fIhex_string\fR is omitted, the ATR is automatically polled from the first active smartcard inserted into a connected reader. Evaluates transmission convention, clock rate conversion (Fi), baud rate adjustment (Di), work ETU, extra guard time, historical bytes, telecom profile classification (GSM, USIM, ISIM, sysmoUSIM), and TCK checksum integrity. Supports \fB--json\fR.
.TP
.BR trace " [" list "|" sniff "]"
Inspect Osmocom SIMtrace 1/2 hardware probes or stream live APDU signaling over GSMTAP (UDP 4729) directly into Wireshark.
.TP
.BR lpac " [" status "|" chip "|" profiles "|" drivers "]"
Interact with the eSIM Local Profile Assistant (lpac) to inspect eUICC chip EID, default SM-DP+ server address, installed MNO profiles, and APDU driver interfaces.
.TP
.B shell
Launch an interactive Osmocom \fBpySim-shell\fR session for smartcard filesystem exploration, file reading, and APDU testing.
.RE
.TP
.BR 5g-sa ", " 5g " [" start "|" stop "|" status "|" add-sub "]"
Manage local Open5GS 5G Standalone core network services:
.RS
.TP
.B start
Start all Open5GS 5G SA network function daemons (NRF, SCP, AMF, SMF, UPF, AUSF, UDM, UDR, PCF, NSSF, BSF).
.TP
.B stop
Gracefully stop all Open5GS core network services.
.TP
.B status
Check the operational status of the Access and Mobility Management Function (AMF) and User Plane Function (UPF).
.TP
.BI add-sub " [" imsi "] [" k "] [" opc "]"
Provision a test SIM subscriber into the Open5GS MongoDB database using \fBopen5gs-dbctl\fR. Defaults to standard testbed credentials if parameters are omitted.
.RE
.TP
.BR scan " [" sctp "|" sip "|" asleap "] [" options "]"
Interactive telecommunications signaling assessment wizard:
.RS
.TP
.B sctp
Launch the Stream Control Transmission Protocol (SCTP) signaling scanner (\fBsctpscan\fR).
.TP
.B sip
Launch the SIPVicious SIP network mapping and enumeration utility (\fBsvmap\fR).
.TP
.B asleap
Launch the PPPoE and MS-CHAPv2 authentication cracker (\fBasleap\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B academy
Launch the TelcoSec Academy interactive field lab portal bridge at \fBhttps://app.telcosec.net\fR.
.TP
.B feedback
Display community support channels and open the SourceForge user reviews portal in the browser.
.TP
.BR completion " [" bash "|" zsh "|" fish "]"
Generate shell autocompletion script for the specified shell.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the release version, build commit, UTC compilation timestamp, and active kernel release.
.SH OPERATIONAL PROFILES
TelcoChiselOS defines two core operational profiles that adjust kernel network filtering:
.TP
.B Lab Mode (rp_filter = 0)
Designed for testbed labs, SDR transmission, and signaling injection. Kernel reverse path filtering is disabled, permitting asymmetric routing, custom GTP-U tunnel encapsulation, and spoofed telecom packet injection.
.TP
.B Field Mode (rp_filter = 1)
Designed for external penetration testing and live operational environments. Strict reverse path filtering is enforced to prevent IP spoofing and maintain network hygiene.
.SH HARDWARE COMPATIBILITY
.B telcosec
identifies and manages the following hardware transceivers:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ettus Research / NI USRP:
B200, B210, B200mini, B205mini, USRP-2900, USRP-2901, X300, X310, N300, N310.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Great Scott Gadgets:
HackRF One, HackRF Jawbreaker, Rad1o Badge.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Nuand:
BladeRF 2.0 micro, BladeRF x40, BladeRF x115.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Lime Microsystems:
LimeSDR USB, LimeSDR Mini.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Realtek:
RTL2832U, RTL2838 (RTL-SDR v3/v4).
.IP \(bu 2
.B Airspy:
Airspy R2, Airspy Mini, Airspy HF+.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Analog Devices:
ADALM-PLUTO, ADALM-PLUTO DFU.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Cellular Modems & SIM Readers:
Qualcomm / Quectel / SIMCom serial AT modems (\fI/dev/ttyUSB*\fR, \fI/dev/ttyACM*\fR) and ISO 7816 PC/SC smartcard readers.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/telcochisel-flavor
Contains the installed distribution flavor name (\fIFlagship Field Edition\fR or \fIModular Lite Edition\fR).
.TP
.I /etc/security/limits.d/99-telcochisel-rt.conf
Configures PAM real-time priority (\fBrtprio 99\fR) and unlimited locked memory (\fBmemlock unlimited\fR).
.TP
.I /sys/module/usbcore/parameters/usbfs_memory_mb
Kernel USBFS buffer parameter. Recommended value is \fB1000\fR MB for continuous SDR streaming.
.TP
.I /proc/sys/vm/nr_hugepages
Configured Linux hugepages count.
.TP
.I /proc/sys/net/ipv4/conf/all/rp_filter
IPv4 reverse path filtering mode flag (0 for Lab Mode, 1 for Field Mode).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/telcosec/index.html
Local offline documentation index.
.TP
.I /usr/share/Nuand/bladeRF/*.rbf
Cached offline FPGA bitstreams for Nuand BladeRF hardware.
.TP
.I /usr/share/uhd/images/*.bin
Cached offline FPGA images for Ettus USRP hardware.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B telcosec check
Run a comprehensive pre-flight system audit.
.TP
.B telcosec hardware
Probe all attached radio transceivers and SIM readers.
.TP
.B telcosec search diameter
Search the tool catalog for Diameter protocol utilities.
.TP
.B telcosec sim atr 3B9F95801FC78031E073FE211B674A4C7380110043
Decode and classify an ISO/IEC 7816-3 Answer-to-Reset from a sysmoUSIM-SJS1 test card.
.TP
.B telcosec sim readers --json
Enumerate all connected PC/SC smartcard readers and detected ATRs in structured JSON.
.TP
.B sudo telcosec 10g tune eth1
Optimize 10GbE network interface \fBeth1\fR with MTU 9000 and 4096 ring descriptors.
.TP
.B sudo telcosec 10g setup eth1 x310-0
Configure \fBeth1\fR for USRP X310 port 0 with IP 192.168.10.1/24 and MTU 9000.
.TP
.B sudo telcosec 5g-sa start
Start local Open5GS 5G Standalone core services.
.TP
.B sudo telcosec 5g-sa add-sub 001010000000001
Provision test subscriber with IMSI 001010000000001 into Open5GS.
.TP
.B source <(telcosec completion bash)
Enable interactive Bash autocompletion in the current terminal session.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error, missing prerequisite, or invalid command arguments.
